From cf5c466a118fbc47750c9e5a25321bdaab71df1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cc <cc@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:20:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: don't abort on lost terminal (EIO) while running TUI

The panic hook restored the terminal and then called the default hook,
which uses eprintln!. When the terminal returned EIO, that eprintln!
panicked again and, with panic = "abort", aborted the process. The
original panic location was lost and the only message left in the core
was "failed printing to stderr".

- set_panic_hook now appends payload + location to clashtui.log with
  OpenOptions append + writeln! on File, ignores write errors, and never
  calls the default hook. No print macros remain in the hook.
- main no longer unwraps the TUI entry points (serve/restore/save); an
  EIO is logged and the process exits cleanly.
- Ratatui's Terminal::drop prints "Failed to show the cursor" via
  eprintln! on error; keep the terminal alive with ManuallyDrop so that
  path is never reached (tui::restore already restores the terminal).
- app.rs startup prompts use write!/writeln! with ignored errors instead
  of print!/eprintln!.
- Replace spawn_blocking(..).await.unwrap() in the tabs with a
  join_blocking helper that turns JoinError into a TUI error state, so an
  unreachable core keeps retrying instead of panicking/aborting.

Reproduced on the reproduced EIO setup: before, SIGABRT with the hook's
own second panic; after, no core, exit 0, log shows only the WebSocket
reconnect warning and "TUI exited with error: Input/output error".
